id: pm-review-github-d686d81c4a08-30
title: Withdrawn lineage observations block response and status for live findings
description: "GH issue #30: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/issues/30 · author @unbraind · state reason completed · created 2026-10-22T21:23:06Z · updated 2026-10-22T22:08:14Z"
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: "gh:unbraind/pm-review#30","github_author:unbraind"
created_at: "2026-10-23T06:04:26.305Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T06:04:26.371Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-23T06:04:26.368Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-22T22:08:14.000Z"
author: pm-github
close_reason: GitHub issue #30 closed
body: "## Reproduced defect\n\nAfter a complete import marks a source observation withdrawn, `responsePlan` still tries to find that source thread in the current PR snapshot. A retained final verdict therefore throws a raw error and blocks both `respond` and `reviewStatus`, including replies for a live sibling in the same confirmed lineage.\n\nTested exact source: `4312cfc43fd5cc53ce412a63b99c9b7889d1c939` from merged [PR #29](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/pull/29). The same response-plan failure also reproduces using `src/respond.ts` from `dc83265891dab4e027019a13cb4e03304203bb15`, so this is an inherited integration gap, not a regression introduced by the final follow-up delta.\n\n## Goal and source evidence\n\nThe [lineage contract](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/blob/4312cfc43fd5cc53ce412a63b99c9b7889d1c939/docs/finding-lineage.md#L38-L67) combines shared effective dispositions with retained withdrawn observations. The canonical [finding-lineage feature](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/blob/4312cfc43fd5cc53ce412a63b99c9b7889d1c939/.agents/pm/features/pm-review-finding-lineage.toon) explicitly preserves source withdrawal history.\n\n[importFindings](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/blob/4312cfc43fd5cc53ce412a63b99c9b7889d1c939/src/tracker.ts#L90-L99) correctly records `review_withdrawn=true`. However, [responsePlan](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/blob/4312cfc43fd5cc53ce412a63b99c9b7889d1c939/src/respond.ts#L49-L55) filters only by repository/PR and decided thread status, without considering withdrawal. Both [respond and reviewStatus](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/blob/4312cfc43fd5cc53ce412a63b99c9b7889d1c939/src/respond.ts#L72-L89) call that planner.\n\n## Sanitized reproduction\n\n1. Import two bot thread observations A and B for `example/project#1`.\n2. Explicitly confirm their lineage while both dispositions agree.\n3. Record a local `fix` on B with a reason and a synthetic 40-character commit SHA. Both projected observations now expose the shared fix; B owns it.\n4. Remove B's thread from a complete synthetic PR snapshot.\n5. Run `importFindings(client, snapshot, findingsOf(snapshot), { snapshotComplete: true })`. Observed receipt: `withdrawn=1`, `withdrawal_checked=true`; A remains live, B is withdrawn, both retain canonical B and verdict `fix`.\n6. Run `responsePlan(snapshot, await reviewItems(client), 'owner', {})`, or the read-only `respond` / `reviewStatus` wrapper.\n\nActual: all three reject with `Recorded verdict thread is missing from the complete PR snapshot`. No live-source plan or status receipt is returned.\n\nControl: passing only the live projected observation to the same unchanged planner produces one correct reply for A. The missing-unwithdrawn-thread guard still throws as expected.\n\nExpected: retain B's evidence and canonical disposition, but do not try to reply to a verified withdrawn source. Continue planning and reporting on live observations. A structured skipped/withdrawn diagnostic is preferable to silently discarding provenance. Missing sources that have not been verified withdrawn should still fail safely.\n\n## Impact and regression criteria\n\nA deleted provider thread with a retained final decision can disable response and status workflows for the entire PR, despite successful complete import and a live confirmed sibling.\n\n- Cover fixed/refused canonical and noncanonical source withdrawal after a complete import.\n- `respond` dry-run and `reviewStatus` must return usable receipts for remaining live sources, without an action targeting the withdrawn thread.\n- Preserve withdrawn body, local reason, audit, lineage and effective disposition.\n- Reappearance restores source eligibility and normal reply deduplication.\n- Keep the guard for unverified missing sources and the default no-withdrawal behavior of partial imports.\n\n## Evidence limits and duplicate check\n\nReproduced on Node v24.19.0 by executing the exact TypeScript source in memory after Node type stripping. Storage, clock and SDK similarity were synthetic; provider mutations were disabled. This verifies control flow and consumer composition, not real SDK persistence/atomicity, installed-package behavior, a live GitHub failure, or a full-suite run. Twelve additional scoped behavioral checks passed.\n\nAll-status issue search, 13 returned all-status PRs, PR #29's review discussion, and the lineage/response canonical feature records were checked. No existing owner for this withdrawal-to-response failure was found. The earlier partial-import withdrawal finding addressed in #29 is different: this reproduction uses a verified complete snapshot."
